##### C. does an alias capture an OTP callback name the language deliberately leaves alone? (bs_otp.erl header: 'a helper that shares a callback's name is never silently captured')
  Capture declares NO behaviour; its public functions are Init/1, HandleCall/2 (arity 2: not a gen_server callback), Start/2.
  baseline exports:
  [{'HandleCall',2},{'Init',1},{'Start',2}]
  alias exports (BS_ALIAS=thin):
  [{'HandleCall',2},{'Init',1},{'Start',2},{handle_call,2},{init,1},{start,2}]
  does gen_server accept the alias-bearing module as a callback module (it has init/1 now, but no handle_call/3)?
  gen_server:start(Capture, 7, []) -> {error,{bad_return_value,7}}
  same call against the BASELINE beam:
  gen_server:start(Capture, 7, []) -> {error,
                                       {undef,
                                        [{'Capture',init,[7],[]},
